How to build graphcoloring.jar
================================

The project uses one helper class, graphcoloring.Tools, packaged into
graphcoloring.jar and attached to the project via the "ProjectJARs"
property in proj/project.json.

From this directory (proj/lib), run:

    javac -d build graphcoloring/Tools.java
    cd build
    jar cf ../graphcoloring.jar graphcoloring
    cd ..

This produces proj/lib/graphcoloring.jar, which ALGator will put on
the classpath of every algorithm in this project (see Output.java, 
which calls graphcoloring.Tools.intArrayToString(), and
IndicatorTest_Check.java / IndicatorTest_NumColors.java, which call
graphcoloring.Tools.isValidColoring() and .numColors()).

After (re)building the jar, re-run the project's "build" step from the
ALGator web UI (or algator.sh) so that all five algorithms are
recompiled against the updated jar.
